## Research
Research completed by parent task #964. Validated against current codebase 2026-03-24.
Dependency #953 (HookWorkerSupervisor) is archived/complete.
Codebase confirms: __call__ calls _count_rejections (sync file I/O, L200) and _get_priority (subprocess.run, L231) before supervisor.schedule(). These block the emit() pipeline.
Approach A (.85 confidence): move eligibility into bg task via _run_with_eligibility wrapper. Smallest diff, KISS-aligned, no new deps.
Existing test suite (43 tests in test_retrospective_hook.py) provides solid baseline for regression.
Risk: 100ms event-loop block in bg task from sync I/O. Acceptable for single-conversation daemon.
Research doc: docs/research/non-blocking-retrospective-hook-handoff.md
Checklist: theoretical validity OK, 8 sources, feasible in stack, clean architecture fit, approach defined, testing defined, doc exists.